# Registers the AI chat-provider selector.
#
# ChatProviderEnvironmentPostProcessor decides whether the chat model comes from Groq or
# from local Ollama, based on whether GROQ_API_KEY is set. It has to run as an environment
# post-processor because Spring AI gates each provider's ChatModel autoconfiguration on
# `spring.ai.model.chat`, and a YAML placeholder cannot express "use this one only when a
# key is present".
#
# The key is org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor — the spring.factories entry
# Spring Boot 4 itself uses for the built-in post-processors.
org.springframework.boot.EnvironmentPostProcessor=\
com.nocteon.nocteon_api.ai.config.ChatProviderEnvironmentPostProcessor